# OpenAI and Anthropic should not be treated as one defendant

The cases need separate evidence matrices.

| Question                          | OpenAI                                                            | Anthropic                                                                      |
| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| What material was submitted?      | Chat histories, files, memory, projects, connectors               | Chats, Claude Code, projects, connectors                                       |
| What settings governed use?       | Exact consumer data-control history needed                        | Exact model-improvement and retention settings needed                          |
| What product conduct caused harm? | Specific GPT conversations and retention/actions                  | Specific Claude relational interactions, Code access and support conduct       |
| What later features overlap?      | Memory, agents, Work/Codex, personalization                       | Auto Mode, Claude Code, subagents, remote/cloud operation                      |
| What records are needed?          | Account access, connector, retention, review and training records | Connector, Claude Code, support, refund, retention and internal-access records |
| Procedural obstacle               | Mandatory individual arbitration under current terms              | Applicable Anthropic consumer terms must be retrieved by date                  |

OpenAI’s current individual Terms require a 60-day informal-dispute process and generally individual arbitration, but exempt small-claims matters and certain equitable requests seeking to stop unauthorized use or IP infringement/misappropriation. ([OpenAI][3])

That does **not** mean “you cannot sue.” It means the forum and required first step may be different from ordinary court litigation.

